course: dictionary
lesson: 311
title: Ancestral: words about family and history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ancestral means connected with your ancestors, the people in your family who lived long before you. Look at the parts: ancest- means ancestor, and -al means connected with. So an ancestral home is a home connected with your ancestors.
explain: «In the dry Southwest the Ancestral Puebloans built houses of stone and adobe in cliffs and canyons.» The capital A shows it is part of a people's name. The clue «Pueblo peoples still live there today» tells you the builders were ancestors, and their families are still in the same place now.
explain: Ancestral has a science meaning too. An ancestral form is an early kind of living thing that later kinds grew from. Birds have ancestral links to dinosaurs, so long ago the family line that led to birds began with earlier, dinosaur-like animals.
fact: Ancestral means connected with your ancestors, the people who lived long before you.
fact: Ancestral is an adjective, so it describes a noun: an ancestral home, an ancestral language, ancestral land.
fact: Ancestral land is land that a family or people has lived on for generations.
fact: In science, ancestral describes an early form of a living thing that later kinds developed from.
fact: The noun is ancestor: one of the people in your family who lived long before you.
exercise: «In the dry Southwest the Ancestral Puebloans built houses of stone and adobe in cliffs and canyons.» What does Ancestral mean here? | Made of wood and glass | Very dry and hot | *Connected with the people who lived long before, the ancestors of today's Pueblo peoples | Connected with people who lived long before, like the builders of these houses
exercise: Ayesha says her ancestral home is the house where her great-grandparents lived. What does ancestral connect the home to? | A new shop | Her friends | Her school | *Her ancestors, the family who lived long before her
exercise: Which word is the noun for a person in your family who lived long before you? | Ancestral | Ancient | *Ancestor | Aunt
test: Birds have ancestral links to dinosaurs. In this science sentence, what does ancestral describe? | A fast animal that lives in the sea | *An early form of a living thing that later kinds developed from | A dinosaur that is still alive today | Something brand new and modern
test: Which is an example of ancestral land? | A road built yesterday | *A field where a family's ancestors lived and farmed for generations | A beach you visited for the first time | A new park opened last year
exam: Why does the text say «Pueblo peoples still live there today» after talking about the Ancestral Puebloans? | Because the houses were built last week | *Because the ancestors built the homes and their descendants still live in the same place | Because the Puebloans are a new team of builders | Because the cliffs are made of adobe
